              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Persisting a caller-controlled `String` or `Bytes` value without a length check lets an attacker grow ledger entries without bound, raising rent and potentially exceeding limits. The detector looks for a visible `.len()` comparison guarding the write."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Unbounded string/bytes persisted from caller input\n\nPersisting a caller-controlled `String` or `Bytes` value without a length check lets an attacker grow ledger entries without bound, raising rent and potentially exceeding limits. The detector looks for a visible `.len()` comparison guarding the write.\n\n### Remediation\n\nReject or truncate values above an explicit maximum before persisting them (for example `if value.len() > MAX { return Err(...) }`). Storing a fixed-size hash instead of the raw value is usually safer.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/persisting-data\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "Persisting a caller-controlled `String` or `Bytes` value without a length check lets an attacker grow ledger entries without bound, raising rent and potentially exceeding limits. The detector looks for a visible `.len()` comparison guarding the write.\n\nRemediation: Reject or truncate values above an explicit maximum before persisting them (for example `if value.len() > MAX { return Err(...) }`). Storing a fixed-size hash instead of the raw value is usually safer."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/storage/persisting-data",
              "id": "SS-025",
              "name": "Unbounded string/bytes persisted from caller input",
              "properties": {
