              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract publishes an event whose topic list includes a function parameter, so the caller influences which topic the event appears under. Off-chain indexers that group or trust events by topic can be fed spoofed, trusted-looking events (for example a fake `transfer` or `admin` event). Topics should identify the event type; caller-controlled values belong in the event data payload. This is a heuristic and reports low confidence."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Event topic derived from a caller-controlled parameter\n\nA contract publishes an event whose topic list includes a function parameter, so the caller influences which topic the event appears under. Off-chain indexers that group or trust events by topic can be fed spoofed, trusted-looking events (for example a fake `transfer` or `admin` event). Topics should identify the event type; caller-controlled values belong in the event data payload. This is a heuristic and reports low confidence.\n\n### Remediation\n\nUse a constant topic (`symbol_short!(\"transfer\")` or `Symbol::new(&env, \"transfer\")`) and put caller-controlled values in the event data payload. If a parameter must appear in a topic, document why and validate it against an allowlist of expected topic values.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/events\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A contract publishes an event whose topic list includes a function parameter, so the caller influences which topic the event appears under. Off-chain indexers that group or trust events by topic can be fed spoofed, trusted-looking events (for example a fake `transfer` or `admin` event). Topics should identify the event type; caller-controlled values belong in the event data payload. This is a heuristic and reports low confidence.\n\nRemediation: Use a constant topic (`symbol_short!(\"transfer\")` or `Symbol::new(&env, \"transfer\")`) and put caller-controlled values in the event data payload. If a parameter must appear in a topic, document why and validate it against an allowlist of expected topic values."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/events",
