            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract entry point calls `require_auth` (or `require_auth_for_args`) inside a loop body. Each iteration repeats an expensive authorization check for the same operation, and the repeated per-item check often means the authorization should be hoisted and bound to the operation's arguments once. This is a resource-efficiency heuristic, not a proof of a security bug."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Redundant require_auth in loop\n\nA contract entry point calls `require_auth` (or `require_auth_for_args`) inside a loop body. Each iteration repeats an expensive authorization check for the same operation, and the repeated per-item check often means the authorization should be hoisted and bound to the operation's arguments once. This is a resource-efficiency heuristic, not a proof of a security bug.\n\n### Remediation\n\nAuthorize once before the loop, for example `admin.require_auth();` followed by the loop, or use `require_auth_for_args` with the complete argument set the operation depends on. If every iteration genuinely authorizes a different actor, document why the per-iteration check is required.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A contract entry point calls `require_auth` (or `require_auth_for_args`) inside a loop body. Each iteration repeats an expensive authorization check for the same operation, and the repeated per-item check often means the authorization should be hoisted and bound to the operation's arguments once. This is a resource-efficiency heuristic, not a proof of a security bug.\n\nRemediation: Authorize once before the loop, for example `admin.require_auth();` followed by the loop, or use `require_auth_for_args` with the complete argument set the operation depends on. If every iteration genuinely authorizes a different actor, document why the per-iteration check is required."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
              "id": "SS-032",
              "name": "Redundant require_auth in loop",
              "properties": {
                "category": "authorization",
                "confidence": "medium",
                "references": [
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security"
                ],
                "remediation": "Authorize once before the loop, for example `admin.require_auth();` followed by the loop, or use `require_auth_for_args` with the complete argument set the operation depends on. If every iteration genuinely authorizes a different actor, document why the per-iteration check is required.",
                "severity": "low"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Redundant require_auth in loop"
              }
            },
