              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A `checked_add`/`checked_sub`/`checked_mul` (or similar) result is discarded or bound without being inspected. Overflow then silently produces `None`, reintroducing the bug the checked API exists to prevent. The detector reports calls whose result is not directly consumed by `?`, `match`, or an `unwrap`/`unwrap_or`-style handler."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Ignored checked-arithmetic result\n\nA `checked_add`/`checked_sub`/`checked_mul` (or similar) result is discarded or bound without being inspected. Overflow then silently produces `None`, reintroducing the bug the checked API exists to prevent. The detector reports calls whose result is not directly consumed by `?`, `match`, or an `unwrap`/`unwrap_or`-style handler.\n\n### Remediation\n\nHandle the checked result: use `?` to propagate it, match on `Some`/`None`, or supply a fallback with `unwrap_or`/`unwrap_or_else`. Never use `checked_*` as a bare statement or discard it into `_`.\n\n### References\n\n- https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/primitive.i128.html#method.checked_add\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A `checked_add`/`checked_sub`/`checked_mul` (or similar) result is discarded or bound without being inspected. Overflow then silently produces `None`, reintroducing the bug the checked API exists to prevent. The detector reports calls whose result is not directly consumed by `?`, `match`, or an `unwrap`/`unwrap_or`-style handler.\n\nRemediation: Handle the checked result: use `?` to propagate it, match on `Some`/`None`, or supply a fallback with `unwrap_or`/`unwrap_or_else`. Never use `checked_*` as a bare statement or discard it into `_`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/primitive.i128.html#method.checked_add",
