              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract entry point calls `require_auth` for two or more distinct actors. Multiple separate approvals in a single operation usually indicate confused authorization semantics: it is hard to tell which actor is actually required, and a missing check elsewhere may be masked. Legitimate multi-party flows exist, so review each finding in context."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Competing authorization calls\n\nA contract entry point calls `require_auth` for two or more distinct actors. Multiple separate approvals in a single operation usually indicate confused authorization semantics: it is hard to tell which actor is actually required, and a missing check elsewhere may be masked. Legitimate multi-party flows exist, so review each finding in context.\n\n### Remediation\n\nPrefer a single, explicit authorization for the actor whose operation this is, or bind all required parties through one documented multi-sig pattern. If the flow genuinely requires several independent approvals, document the policy and suppress the finding with a justified inline directive.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A contract entry point calls `require_auth` for two or more distinct actors. Multiple separate approvals in a single operation usually indicate confused authorization semantics: it is hard to tell which actor is actually required, and a missing check elsewhere may be masked. Legitimate multi-party flows exist, so review each finding in context.\n\nRemediation: Prefer a single, explicit authorization for the actor whose operation this is, or bind all required parties through one documented multi-sig pattern. If the flow genuinely requires several independent approvals, document the policy and suppress the finding with a justified inline directive."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
              "id": "SS-037",
              "name": "Competing authorization calls",
              "properties": {
