              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A contract entry point performs `require_auth` (or `require_auth_for_args`) inside a loop body in a position that does not clearly cover every iteration: the check is conditional, or it runs only after a state-changing operation. A single check in that position can leave later iterations or earlier side effects unauthorized. Unconditional checks at the top of a loop are ambiguous and are deliberately not reported by this rule."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "## Authorization check inside a loop\n\nA contract entry point performs `require_auth` (or `require_auth_for_args`) inside a loop body in a position that does not clearly cover every iteration: the check is conditional, or it runs only after a state-changing operation. A single check in that position can leave later iterations or earlier side effects unauthorized. Unconditional checks at the top of a loop are ambiguous and are deliberately not reported by this rule.\n\n### Remediation\n\nAuthorize the actor before any state change and outside any conditional branch that can skip iterations, or authorize each distinct actor explicitly for every loop item with `require_auth_for_args`. Document intentional per-item authorization.\n\n### References\n\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization\n- https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security",
                "text": "A contract entry point performs `require_auth` (or `require_auth_for_args`) inside a loop body in a position that does not clearly cover every iteration: the check is conditional, or it runs only after a state-changing operation. A single check in that position can leave later iterations or earlier side effects unauthorized. Unconditional checks at the top of a loop are ambiguous and are deliberately not reported by this rule.\n\nRemediation: Authorize the actor before any state change and outside any conditional branch that can skip iterations, or authorize each distinct actor explicitly for every loop item with `require_auth_for_args`. Document intentional per-item authorization."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
              "id": "SS-041",
              "name": "Authorization check inside a loop",
              "properties": {
                "category": "authorization",
                "confidence": "medium",
                "references": [
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security/authorization",
                  "https://developers.stellar.org/docs/learn/encyclopedia/security"
                ],
                "remediation": "Authorize the actor before any state change and outside any conditional branch that can skip iterations, or authorize each distinct actor explicitly for every loop item with `require_auth_for_args`. Document intentional per-item authorization.",
                "severity": "medium"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Authorization check inside a loop"
              }
            }
